---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
const lastUpdated = "August 2026";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Comprehensive information regarding how Pixelquil and third party advertising partners like Google AdSense utilize cookies and tracking technologies."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20">
    <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-brand-600">
      Cookie Policy
    </span>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">Cookie Policy and Tracking Disclosure</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Understanding Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Cookies are compact text files stored on your computer or mobile device by web browsers when visiting online platforms. They allow sites to recognize returning visits, store essential configuration preferences, and enable external advertising networks to serve relevant promotional content.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">First Party Cookies and Browser Storage</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Pixelquil does not set first party tracking cookies or profile building technologies on your device. All utilities operate client side directly in your web browser environment without requiring user logins or persistent session identifiers.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Some tools may use temporary local browser storage to save your working active state, such as remembering a converted color format or active editor code snippet during a single browser session. This data remains strictly stored on your local device and is never transmitted to outside analytics servers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Google AdSense and Third Party Advertising</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Pixelquil relies on third party vendors, including Google AdSense, to serve display advertisements when users visit the website. Third party vendors use cookies to serve ads based on a user prior visits to this website or other websites across the Internet.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Google use of advertising cookies enables it and its network partners to serve tailored ads based on browsing interactions across participating digital properties. The DoubleClick cookie is utilized by Google to measure campaign performance and prevent duplicate display units.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You can inspect your personalized advertising settings or opt out of targeted ad serving by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline font-medium" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>. To learn more about how Google handles information gathered through partner web platforms, consult <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline font-medium" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Partner Sites Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">User Consent and Cookie Control Options</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Most web browsers automatically accept cookies by default, but you can modify browser settings to decline third party advertising cookies, clear historical tracking data, or warn you whenever a website attempts to place a cookie file.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Blocking or clearing third party cookies will alter advertisement relevancy but will not restrict your access to any tool, converter, or guide published on Pixelquil, as our software utilities run independently of external tracking setups.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You can also opt out of third party vendor use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting the consumer choice portal at <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline font-medium" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">About Ads Consumer Choice Page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Policy Inquiries</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you have questions regarding our compliance with digital advertising standards or cookie usage disclosures, please send a message via our <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline font-medium">contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>